WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 5 Student Video
Unit 2, Lesson 1: Worldview

1
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:12.340
Imagine you decide to try and navigate through a life-sized maze.

2
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:18.400
Personally, I have no sense of direction and easily get lost, confused, and

3
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:18.880
frustrated.

4
00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:24.360
In fact, I'd probably rather sit alone for an hour and just think and do nothing

5
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:26.680
than try to make it through a maze alone.

6
00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:31.920
But if you had to go through a maze, what would make it easier to navigate?

7
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:37.260
Well, a guide would be helpful. It could help us know which steps to take as we try

8
00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.460
to get through the maze. A compass would be really nice.

9
00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.360
In fact, a compass would probably prevent us from getting lost, which is probably

10
00:00:44.360 --> 00:00:49.860
what would happen to me. Or a map would be super helpful, because a map would help

11
00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:53.820
us know exactly the path to be on from beginning to end.

12
00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.600
Essentially, what we would be looking for is someone or something to help us make it

13
00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.860
through the maze safely. We

14
00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:27.260
constantly make choices every day based on our worldview.

15
00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:32.000
Choices about how we treat people, how we spend our money, how we spend our time,

16
00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.440
whether we believe in God or not.

17
00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.600
And these choices lead us on a certain path.

18
00:01:37.900 --> 00:01:42.180
And in the end, we find ourselves at a specific destination.

19
00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:47.820
Now, there's no physical map for the maze of life, but we all have a mental map, a

20
00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:52.060
worldview, which is a set of beliefs that we have that helps us interpret the world

21
00:01:52.060 --> 00:01:53.760
around us. How accurate and live in reality.

22
00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.060
So here's the critical question.

23
00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:59.940
How accurate is your mental map of reality?

24
00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:01.280
Your worldview?

25
00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:05.740
I mean, think about it. If you have a physical map and it doesn't match up, you're

26
00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:10.840
going to get lost and confused. But if your map does match up, you can make it

27
00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:15.900
through the maze successfully. We all carry around ideas which are part of our

28
00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:19.240
worldview, which shape our daily choices.

29
00:02:19.800 --> 00:02:25.060
Whether you're a Christian, an atheist, Buddhist, a Hindu, we all have a belief

30
00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:27.260
system that shapes the way that we live.

31
00:02:27.520 --> 00:02:30.200
You see, the question is not, do we have a worldview?

32
00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:34.320
The question is, what is our worldview and where did it come from?

33
00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.440
From friends? From tradition? From family?

34
00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.280
From culture? Where does our worldview originate?

35
00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:46.460
With all these influences on our worldview, it's going to be critical to take a

36
00:02:46.460 --> 00:02:49.220
moment and examine our belief system more carefully.

37
00:02:49.240 --> 00:02:50.240
There

38
00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:04.760
are a lot of different ways to examine the concept of a worldview and our own

39
00:03:04.760 --> 00:03:06.260
worldviews in particular.

40
00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:12.540
Perhaps most helpful will be to consider four big questions that every worldview

41
00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:16.360
has to answer. First, what is real?

42
00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:22.600
What exists? Is reality only the physical world that we can touch, taste,

43
00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:28.580
see, and feel? Or is there a spiritual realm beyond the physical world?

44
00:03:29.260 --> 00:03:33.880
Is a human being just a body? Or is there also a soul?

45
00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:39.220
Second, what is man? What does it mean to be human?

46
00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:44.400
Are we the product of blind evolutionary forces within nature?

47
00:03:45.040 --> 00:03:50.120
Or are we a part of the larger God consciousness and interconnected with all of

48
00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:55.600
reality? Or are we the personal creation of loving God who made us

49
00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:59.460
in His image? Third, what happens at death?

50
00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:03.160
Where do we go, if anywhere, when we die?

51
00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:07.880
Maybe this is all there is, and that death is final.

52
00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:11.460
When your heart stops beating, that's it.

53
00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:17.820
Or maybe you enter into some state of reincarnation until you finally reach nirvana.

54
00:04:18.460 --> 00:04:24.000
Or maybe when you die, you face judgment before God and go to either heaven or hell

55
00:04:24.000 --> 00:04:29.900
for eternity. Every belief system has some claim about what happens when we

56
00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:30.080
die.

57
00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:34.620
And fourth, what is the basis for right and wrong?

58
00:04:34.860 --> 00:04:40.540
Where does morality come from? Some believe that morality is relative, that there's

59
00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:44.480
no absolute standard outside of us, and that right and wrong comes from the

60
00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:50.320
individual or society. Others would point to karma, that we get rewarded or punished

61
00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:54.580
from actions we've done in the past, and they carry on into the future.

62
00:04:54.960 --> 00:04:59.580
Whereas others believe that there's a standard outside of us, an objective standard

63
00:04:59.580 --> 00:05:04.800
that comes from either God's character or God's commands, which determines right

64
00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:09.120
from wrong. So why bother to think so deeply about our worldview?

65
00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:12.780
As Christians, isn't our worldview already set?

66
00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:18.200
Well, interestingly, and very importantly, studies show that people who describe

67
00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:22.940
themselves as Christians, in other words, they check that box on a survey, live no

68
00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:25.840
differently from people who do not.

69
00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:30.780
But there's a segment of people who describe themselves as Christians that live

70
00:05:30.780 --> 00:05:35.020
differently. It's the Christians with a biblical worldview.

71
00:05:35.900 --> 00:05:40.740
So that means if you want to live with the power of the gospel in your life, you

72
00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:44.360
need to see the world through the lens that Jesus saw it.

73
00:05:45.320 --> 00:05:51.120
If you see the world as Jesus did, in terms of our four big worldview questions and

74
00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:54.320
more, you'll be far more likely to live like Jesus.

75
00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:59.360
And if you live the way that Jesus wanted you to, you'll be far more likely to

76
00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:04.520
experience the freedom that he promised to those who follow him on the path of life.

